SUMMARY:Upcoming Exhibit - Trans Magic: Owning Our Stories of Strength and Resilience
DESCRIPTION:August 6 – 30\, 2026\nPetaluma Historical Library & Museum\n20 4th Street (Corner of 4th & B Street)\nHours:  Thursday – Sunday\,  10 a.m. – 4 p.m.\nAdmission Free\,  Donations Appreciated \n\n\nA community-curated exhibit celebrating the creativity\, organizing\, and history of trans and gender-expansive people in the North Bay and greater Bay Area. The exhibit traces a direct line from the gender-bending creativity of early 20th-century Vaudeville\, to the radical resistance of the groundbreaking 1966 Compton’s Cafeteria Riot\, and finally to the modern triumphs of community groups bringing joyful connection today.
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/upcoming-exhibit-trans-magic-owning-our-stories-of-strength-and-resilience/
LOCATION:Petaluma Historical Library & Museum\, 20 4th St\, Petaluma\, CA\, United States
CATEGORIES:Upcoming Exhibit
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/TransMagic.png
END:VEVENT
